<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:zap="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Zapit;assembly=OpenRigs.Zapit"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:zdq="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Opto.ZapitBonsai;assembly=OpenRigs.Opto.ZapitBonsai"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Zapit's setup phase, between launch and Go, inside ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's Zapit group: the protocol is lib-open-rigs' docs/zapit-setup-protocol.md. Declares the device Zapit-Main's commands (DeclareDeviceControls): Zapit-Main.Setup (args: a grid run folder in RigConfigs\&lt;RIG&gt;\pending holding the agent's grid.json) points the galvos at each point, saving point_NNNN.png and background_K.png there (ZapitSetupCapture); Zapit-Main.Still (args: a new .png in pending) saves the next camera frame, laser off; Zapit-Main.LoadBank (args: the bank's Settings_ZapitBank_&lt;DateTime&gt;.json in pending) loads it into ZapitDaq (ZapitSetupCapture checks the path), which publishes it on Zapit.Bank; Zapit-Main.LaserOff zeroes every line at once, before or after Go. Zapit-Main.Aim (args: xVolts,yVolts,laserVolts) points the beam by hand, reported on its own metric Zapit-Main.Aim ("Aiming &lt;volts&gt;", "Off Go" or "Refused &lt;why&gt;") so the Setup metric keeps BankLoaded; refused at rig.yml zapit.ceilingMw 0, above laserMinMaxControlVolts[1] (both from ZapitRig), above the ceiling's volts (Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts, ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's launch property LaserCeilingVolts) or during a grid run or still; a grid's laserVolts is held to the same rules; at Go a beam still aimed is zeroed, and a grid run or still in progress refused with the lines zeroed. A still with no camera frame in 2 s is refused. Setup, Still and LoadBank are taken until Go (ExperimentGo) and ignored after it. Each stage is reported as the metric Zapit-Main.Setup: "Pointing &lt;folder&gt;", "FramesSaved &lt;folder&gt;", "StillSaved &lt;png&gt;", "Loading &lt;json&gt;", "BankLoaded &lt;json&gt;" or "Refused &lt;why&gt;", each stage before its command goes to ZapitDaq, whose answer (BankLoaded comes back inside LoadBank) must not be overwritten by it; a refused request leaves the workflow running. A grid.json camera block's exposure and gain go to the Zapit camera with the run's first point, and its session settings back with the run's end, on Camera-Zapit.Settings (ZapitCamera's ZapitPylonCapture). Zapit-Main.Play (args: condition,powerMw,seconds) is Play Condition (ZapitPlay; open_rigs.zapit.play drives the sequence): ZapitDaq's own Arm of that condition from the loaded bank as trial 0, refused (never an error) with no bank, a play already armed, the laser disabled, or a condition, power or duration the bank and maxTrialSeconds cannot play, reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Play (Arming, Armed, Playing, Ended, Off or Refused); Zapit-Main.Trigger (args: on, else off) raises or clears the ZapitTrigger line on BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands (SetZapitTriggerLine; the twin's trigger with on), which starts the armed play on the NI DAQ's trigger terminal as a trial's trigger does; the line is cleared by LaserOff, by the play's end (its own, a stop or a Zero) and at Go with a play still armed (its lines zeroed), and when the workflow stops (the board piece's ClearOutputsOnStop). Play and Trigger are taken until Go and ignored after it. Zapit-Main.Crop (args: x,y,w,h in pixels of the camera's frame, or full) cuts the Zapit camera's shown and recorded frame (ZapitCropRequest, on Camera-Zapit.Settings to ZapitCamera), reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Crop ("Cropped &lt;x,y,w,h&gt;", "Full Frame" or "Refused &lt;why&gt;"); taken until Go only, so the recording, which starts at Go, keeps one frame size. Stills and grid runs save Camera-Zapit.Data's Still, the whole frame (a grid run's at Mono8's scale), never the cropped Image. A bank ZapitDaq refuses (hash, sample rate, a volt outside +/-10 V) stops the workflow naming it. Needs ControlEvents, ExperimentGo, RigFile, ZapitRig, Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts, Zapit.Commands, Zapit.Events, Zapit.Bank, Camera-Zapit.Settings, Camera-Zapit.Data, ZapitTriggerLine and BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands from the workflow.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Setup</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Still</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Data</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Value.Still</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>RigFile</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Name>PendingFolder</scr:Name>
        <scr:Expression>it.Substring(0, it.LastIndexOf(Convert.ToChar(92)) + 1) + "pending"</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="PendingFolder" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitSetupCapture">
          <zap:PendingFolder>UNMAPPED</zap:PendingFolder>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Setup</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>LoadBank</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>LaserOff</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:CreateZapitDaqCommand" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>BankLoaded?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Kind == "BankLoaded"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Bank</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Bank</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Expression>"BankLoaded " + JsonPath</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Setup</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:DeclareDeviceControls">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Parameters />
          <orcl:Commands>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Setup</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Run the scanner grid in the pending folder named (its grid.json): a frame per point, then laser-off backgrounds. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Still</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Save the next Zapit camera frame, laser off, as the pending .png named. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>LoadBank</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Load the session's bank (Settings_ZapitBank_&lt;DateTime&gt;.json) into ZapitDaq. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>LaserOff</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Stop any Zapit output at once: galvos, laser and LED at 0 V.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Aim</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Point the beam by hand: args xVolts,yVolts,laserVolts (the agent's, through the scanner fit and laser curve). Refused at ceilingMw 0, above laserMinMaxControlVolts[1] or during a grid run or still; LaserOff ends it. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Play</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Play Condition: args condition,powerMw,seconds. Arms that condition's trial from the loaded bank as ZapitDaq arms a task's (trial 0), at one of its powers (at most ceilingMw), lasting seconds with its ramp; Trigger on starts it. Reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Play (Arming, Armed, Playing, Ended, Off or Refused). Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Trigger</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>The ZapitTrigger line (and the masking light): args on raises it, starting an armed play; anything else clears it. Cleared too by LaserOff and when the play ends. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Crop</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>The Zapit camera's shown and recorded frame cut to args x,y,w,h (pixels of the camera's frame; w and h even), or the whole frame for full or none; the stills stay whole. Reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Crop (Cropped, Full or Refused). Before Go only: the recording starts at Go, so its frame size is fixed from there.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
          </orcl:Commands>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCamera?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Camera != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Camera</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Settings</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Aim</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ZapitRig</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="CeilingMw" Selector="LaserCeilingMw" />
          <Property Name="LaserMaxVolts" Selector="LaserMaxControlVolts" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>Aim?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Aim</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Aim</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>SetupStep?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>!Aim</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="LaserCeilingVolts" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Play</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ZapitRig</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="MaxTrialSeconds" Selector="MaxTrialSeconds" />
          <Property Name="CeilingMw" Selector="LaserCeilingMw" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>PlayCondition</Name>
        <Description>Play Condition before Go (open_rigs.zapit.play drives it): each Zapit-Main.Play request (condition,powerMw,seconds) becomes ZapitDaq's own Arm of that condition from the loaded bank (trial 0), or is refused; its stages reported as Zapit-Main.Play before the Arm goes to ZapitDaq.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitPlay">
          <zap:MaxTrialSeconds>0</zap:MaxTrialSeconds>
          <zap:CeilingMw>0</zap:CeilingMw>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Play</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>PlayOver?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Stage == "Ended" || Stage == "Off"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>The play over (Ended, or Off at Go): the ZapitTrigger line cleared here, a backstop to the agent's own clear.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Trigger</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>On?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Trim() == "on"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Play Condition's start: the ZapitTrigger line raised, as a trial's trigger raises it (the masking light with it).</Description>
        <Set>true</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>TwinTrigger</Name>
        <Description>The simulated twin's trigger edge with the line, as ZapitDaqTrials sends it; the NI DAQ ignores it.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zdq:ZapitTwinTrigger" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>Off?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Trim() != "on"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Zapit-Main.Trigger off (anything but on): the ZapitTrigger line cleared.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Zapit-Main.LaserOff before Go: the ZapitTrigger line cleared with the outputs zeroed.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Crop</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>CropRequest</Name>
        <Description>Zapit-Main.Crop before Go: the shown and recorded frame's crop (x,y,w,h, or the whole frame), reported as Zapit-Main.Crop and sent to the camera on Camera-Zapit.Settings. After Go none is taken: the mp4 starts at Go at the crop then.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitCropRequest" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Crop</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCamera?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
